bot.log
bot.send
.env
bot.startup
bot.stdout.log

# Libera.Chat instance runtime (2nd bot: same code, own nick/FIFO/logs/env).
# bot.trust.libera IS tracked (nick + public cloak, like bot.trust).
.env.libera
bot.send.libera
bot.startup.libera
bot.libera.log
bot.libera.stdout.log

# IRCnet instance runtime (3rd bot: same code, own nick/FIFO/logs).
# bot.trust.ircnet IS tracked — it is empty BY DESIGN and the reasoning in it
# is the point, not the entries. .env.ircnet carries no NICKSERV_PASS (IRCnet
# has no services at all) but stays untracked like its twins, so the pattern
# never becomes "a .env in this repo is safe to commit".
.env.ircnet
bot.send.ircnet
bot.startup.ircnet
bot.ircnet.log
bot.ircnet.stdout.log
aup_watchdog.log
roll_counter.log
chanstats.log
rolls.json
rolls.json.bak-*
scrub.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Raw source PNGs from Gemini — only compressed JPEGs under docs/img/ are committed
docs/img/*.png

# Private — channel-specific memory, not for public repo
memory/

# Host-specific Claude Code settings (paths, WebFetch domains)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Reference material (private copies of Azzurra helpers docs, etc.)
refs/

# Scratch / transient workspace crud — dump here, gitignored wholesale
tmp/
*.lock

# Host-local automation helpers (cron scripts + their logs) — not for public repo
tools/


# Petition sidecar private state (nick+host dedup, PII — never synced/committed)
firma_state.json
firma_counter.log

# sniffo message-stats sidecar — not tracked here (lives in its own folder);
# its DB, slug salt, logs and rendered per-channel output are all PII.
sniffo_stats/
systemd/vjt-claude-sniffo-stats.service

# Dinner poll sidecar private state (nick + vote) — not for public repo
cena_state.json
cena_counter.log

# Impiccato sidecar — state, logs and the question bank itself, all untracked.
# The state is a scoreboard keyed by nick, so it is PII. The BANK is out for a
# different reason (vjt's call, 2026-08-25): its `goliardia` set answers with
# bestemmie, which belong in the channel and not in a public repo. The code
# ships, the content stays local: drop your own impiccato_domande.json beside
# impiccato.py — without one it exits rather than starting empty.
impiccato_domande.json
impiccato_state.json
impiccato_state.*.json
impiccato.*.log

# !list gag sidecar runtime log
list_sidecar.log
next_state.json
next_counter.log
